@startuml
' Purpose: Patient journey lifecycle and phase progression
' Source of truth:
'   src/api/schemas/journey.ts
'   src/api/service/patientJourneys.ts
'   src/api/service/journeyDates.ts

title Patient Journey Lifecycle - State Diagram

state ACTIVE
state SUSPENDED
state COMPLETED

[*] --> ACTIVE : assignPatientJourney / startNextPhase\n(pausedAt=null, totalPausedDays=0)

ACTIVE --> SUSPENDED : pauseJourney\n(records pausedAt=now())
SUSPENDED --> ACTIVE : resumeJourney\n(totalPausedDays += elapsedDays,\npausedAt=null)
ACTIVE --> COMPLETED : startNextPhase (previous phase)\n/ cancelJourney (has data)
SUSPENDED --> COMPLETED : cancelJourney (has data,\npausedAt=null)
ACTIVE --> [*] : cancelJourney (no data)\njourney deleted
SUSPENDED --> [*] : cancelJourney (no data)\njourney deleted

note right of SUSPENDED
  Step dates shift dynamically by
  totalPausedDays + currentPauseDays
  (computeTotalPauseShift; no store
  write until resumeJourney, which also
  re-dates the journey's Instructions)
end note

note right of ACTIVE
  Late enrolment (joinedAt > startDate):
  closed-window steps get system
  REMOVE_STEP modifications and past
  instructions are created CANCELLED
  (cancelReason = LATE_JOIN).
end note

note bottom of ACTIVE
  Phase progression is handled by
  startNextPhase(...): previous journey
  becomes COMPLETED and a new journey is
  created in the same episode with phaseType
  and transition (fromJourneyId, trigger).
end note

@enduml
